        'NETGEAR Nighthawk M3 assessed: mobile 5G router with Wi-Fi 6 and battery for your own Wi-Fi on the road, on sites and at fairs. Safer than open Wi-Fi.',
        'The Nighthawk M3 is a mobile 5G router with a battery and Wi-Fi 6. With a SIM card it creates your own encrypted Wi-Fi anywhere, for laptop, tablet and colleagues.',
        [['Mobile', '5G and LTE, SIM card required'], ['Wi-Fi', 'Wi-Fi 6'], ['Power', 'battery, also on mains'], ['Suited to', 'trade fairs, sites, holiday flats, backup line']],
        [['Do I need a separate contract?', 'Yes, a data SIM. Many providers offer cheap second cards or data-only plans.'], ['Why not just a phone hotspot?', 'The router lasts longer, serves more devices stably and spares the phone battery.'], ['Does it work as a DSL backup?', 'Yes, as an emergency network for the office it is very handy.']],
        $bodyEn('Open hotel or trade-fair Wi-Fi is slow and insecure. Your own 5G router gives you a network you control.', ['Your own encrypted Wi-Fi anywhere', 'Several devices at once', 'Also an emergency network when the landline fails'], ['Needs its own SIM with data', 'Speed depends on the local mobile network'], 'Teams at trade fairs and on sites, frequent travellers and offices that want a backup line.'),
